prompt_messages.content:
Note digests:
{"note_id":50,"note_type":"Breast Imaging Report","summary":"Screening mammogram identified a developing asymmetry in the left breast, and diagnostic imaging demonstrated a 2.3 cm irregular hypoechoic mass with suspicious features, resulting in a BI‑RADS 5 assessment and recommendation for biopsy, which was completed.","flags":["screening mammogram","diagnostic imaging","BI-RADS 5","core biopsy","breast mass"]}
{"note_id":51,"note_type":"Pathology Report","summary":"Invasive mammary carcinoma with ductal features was identified on a left breast core biopsy, measuring at least 1.1 cm and associated with intermediate‑grade ductal carcinoma in situ; estrogen and progesterone receptors are positive and HER2 is negative, with no lymphovascular invasion noted. Definitive tumor size and nodal status will be assessed at excision.","flags":["breast biopsy","invasive ductal carcinoma","DCIS","hormone receptor positive","HER2 negative"]}
{"note_id":52,"note_type":"Surgical Oncology Consultation","summary":"Patient evaluated after biopsy confirming left breast cancer; MRI shows a solitary lesion with no multifocal or contralateral disease, staged clinically as cT2 cN0 cM0; plan for left lumpectomy with sentinel lymph node biopsy was discussed and selected.","flags":["left breast cancer","lumpectomy","sentinel lymph node biopsy","clinical staging","MRI findings","surgical oncology"]}
{"note_id":53,"note_type":"Operative Pathology Report","summary":"Left breast lumpectomy with sentinel lymph node biopsy was performed, revealing a 2.4 cm invasive ductal carcinoma, grade 2, with associated intermediate‑grade DCIS; margins are negative for both invasive cancer and DCIS and all three sentinel nodes are negative, resulting in pathologic stage pT2 pN0(sn). Post‑operative recovery was uncomplicated aside from mild axillary soreness and a small resolving seroma.","flags":["lumpectomy","sentinel lymph node biopsy","invasive ductal carcinoma","DCIS","negative margins","pT2 pN0"]}
{"note_id":54,"note_type":"Medical Oncology Consultation","summary":"The patient had an initial medical oncology consultation to discuss her resected left‑breast invasive carcinoma, which is hormone‑receptor positive, HER2‑negative, node‑negative, and larger than 2 cm. A genomic assay was ordered to assess potential benefit of adjuvant chemotherapy. Staging scans were deferred because there are no systemic symptoms.","flags":["breast cancer","hormone receptor positive","HER2-negative","node-negative","genomic assay","adjuvant chemotherapy","oncology consultation"]}
{"note_id":55,"note_type":"Systemic Therapy Note","summary":"Genomic assay showed intermediate-high risk and adjuvant chemotherapy with docetaxel/cyclophosphamide was initiated; the patient tolerated the first cycle with expected fatigue and metallic taste. A radiation oncology referral was placed for whole‑breast radiation after chemotherapy, with endocrine therapy planned thereafter. The patient was counseled that the invasive component, not the in‑situ component, drives prognosis and treatment planning.","flags":["genomic assay","adjuvant chemotherapy","docetaxel/cyclophosphamide","radiation referral","endocrine therapy","invasive carcinoma"]}
{"note_id":56,"note_type":"Clinical History","summary":"The note records the patient's past medical history of hypertension, hyperlipidemia, and a prior benign breast cyst aspiration, with no history of breast cancer. The patient denies nipple discharge, skin ulceration, dyspnea, and focal neurologic symptoms and has an ECOG performance status of 0. Routine pre‑chemotherapy CBC and CMP were adequate for treatment.","flags":["hypertension","hyperlipidemia","benign breast cyst aspiration","ECOG 0","pre‑chemotherapy labs"]}

