Clinical notes:
{"note_id":50,"date":"2025-02-20","note_type":"Breast Imaging Report","content":"Screening mammogram on 2025-02-06 showed a developing asymmetry in the upper outer left breast. Diagnostic mammogram with targeted ultrasound on 2025-02-14 demonstrated a 2.3 cm irregular hypoechoic mass at 2 o'clock, 6 cm from the nipple, with angular margins and posterior shadowing. Left axillary nodes were not enlarged by imaging criteria. Impression was BI-RADS 5, highly suspicious for malignancy. Ultrasound-guided core biopsy was recommended and completed on 2025-02-20.","summary":"Screening mammogram identified a developing asymmetry in the left breast, and diagnostic imaging demonstrated a 2.3 cm irregular hypoechoic mass with suspicious features, resulting in a BI‑RADS 5 assessment and recommendation for biopsy, which was completed.","concepts":{"cancer":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":50,"text":"Impression was BI-RADS 5, highly suspicious for malignancy"}]},"metastasis":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"surgery":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"chemotherapy":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"radiation":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"lymph_nodes_removed":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]}},"cancer_status":null,"cancer_mentions":[],"flags":["screening mammogram","diagnostic imaging","BI-RADS 5","core biopsy","breast mass"]}
{"note_id":51,"date":"2025-02-24","note_type":"Pathology Report","content":"Specimen: Left breast, 2 o'clock mass, core biopsy.\nFinal Diagnosis: Invasive mammary carcinoma with ductal features. The invasive carcinoma involves multiple cores and measures at least 1.1 cm in the submitted tissue. Associated ductal carcinoma in situ is present, intermediate nuclear grade. Lymphovascular invasion is not identified in this biopsy material. Estrogen receptor positive, progesterone receptor positive, HER2 negative by immunohistochemistry. Comment: Overall findings are most in keeping with a primary breast invasive ductal carcinoma. This biopsy establishes malignancy; definitive size and nodal status are deferred to excision.","summary":"Invasive mammary carcinoma with ductal features was identified on a left breast core biopsy, measuring at least 1.1 cm and associated with intermediate‑grade ductal carcinoma in situ; estrogen and progesterone receptors are positive and HER2 is negative, with no lymphovascular invasion noted. Definitive tumor size and nodal status will be assessed at excision.","concepts":{"cancer":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":51,"text":"Invasive mammary carcinoma with ductal features"}]},"metastasis":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"surgery":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"chemotherapy":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"radiation":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"lymph_nodes_removed":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]}},"cancer_status":["current"],"cancer_mentions":[{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":51,"text":"Invasive mammary carcinoma with ductal features"},{"note_id":51,"text":"Associated ductal carcinoma in situ is present, intermediate nuclear grade"}],"status":"current","affected_tissue":"left breast","metastasis":false}],"flags":["breast biopsy","invasive ductal carcinoma","DCIS","hormone receptor positive","HER2 negative"]}
{"note_id":52,"date":"2025-03-03","note_type":"Surgical Oncology Consultation","content":"Seen 2025-03-03 after biopsy confirmation of left breast cancer. MRI from 2025-02-27 shows enhancement corresponding to the known lesion only, without multifocal or contralateral disease. No chest wall invasion. Clinical stage reviewed as cT2 cN0 cM0. We discussed breast-conserving surgery versus mastectomy. Given localized disease and patient preference, plan was for left lumpectomy with sentinel lymph node biopsy. Differential considerations from the original imaging report such as radial scar or complex sclerosing lesion are no longer relevant after tissue diagnosis. No evidence of inflammatory breast cancer on exam.","summary":"Patient evaluated after biopsy confirming left breast cancer; MRI shows a solitary lesion with no multifocal or contralateral disease, staged clinically as cT2 cN0 cM0; plan for left lumpectomy with sentinel lymph node biopsy was discussed and selected.","concepts":{"cancer":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":52,"text":"left breast cancer"}]},"metastasis":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"surgery":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":52,"text":"left lumpectomy"}]},"chemotherapy":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"radiation":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"lymph_nodes_removed":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":52,"text":"sentinel lymph node biopsy"}]}},"cancer_status":["current"],"cancer_mentions":[{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":52,"text":"left breast cancer"},{"note_id":52,"text":"cT2 cN0 cM0"}],"status":"current","affected_tissue":"left breast","metastasis":false}],"flags":["left breast cancer","lumpectomy","sentinel lymph node biopsy","clinical staging","MRI findings","surgical oncology"]}
{"note_id":53,"date":"2025-03-18","note_type":"Operative Pathology Report","content":"Procedure performed 2025-03-18: left breast lumpectomy with sentinel lymph node biopsy. Final surgical pathology shows invasive ductal carcinoma, 2.4 cm, Nottingham grade 2, with associated intermediate-grade DCIS. Margins negative for invasive carcinoma and DCIS. Three sentinel lymph nodes examined, all negative for carcinoma (0/3). Pathologic stage pT2 pN0(sn). Post-op recovery uncomplicated aside from mild axillary soreness and a small resolving seroma.","summary":"Left breast lumpectomy with sentinel lymph node biopsy was performed, revealing a 2.4 cm invasive ductal carcinoma, grade 2, with associated intermediate‑grade DCIS; margins are negative for both invasive cancer and DCIS and all three sentinel nodes are negative, resulting in pathologic stage pT2 pN0(sn). Post‑operative recovery was uncomplicated aside from mild axillary soreness and a small resolving seroma.","concepts":{"cancer":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":53,"text":"invasive ductal carcinoma"}]},"metastasis":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"surgery":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":53,"text":"left breast lumpectomy"}]},"chemotherapy":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"radiation":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"lymph_nodes_removed":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":53,"text":"sentinel lymph node biopsy"}]}},"cancer_status":["current"],"cancer_mentions":[{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":53,"text":"Procedu{ "}],"status":"current","affected_tissue":"left breast","metastasis":false}],"flags":["lumpectomy","sentinel lymph node biopsy","invasive ductal carcinoma","DCIS","negative margins","pT2 pN0"]}
{"note_id":54,"date":"2025-04-02","note_type":"Medical Oncology Consultation","content":"Initial med onc visit 2025-04-02. We reviewed that she has a resected left breast primary with hormone receptor positive, HER2-negative disease and node-negative status after sentinel node sampling. Because the tumor is over 2 cm and the patient is otherwise fit, genomic assay was sent to help estimate benefit of adjuvant chemotherapy. There is no suggestion in the record of a purely in situ process or benign lesion; treatment recommendations are being made for an invasive breast cancer. Staging scans were not ordered because she has no bone pain, cough, weight loss, or abnormal liver tests, and presentation remains consistent with localized disease.","summary":"The patient had an initial medical oncology consultation to discuss her resected left‑breast invasive carcinoma, which is hormone‑receptor positive, HER2‑negative, node‑negative, and larger than 2 cm. A genomic assay was ordered to assess potential benefit of adjuvant chemotherapy. Staging scans were deferred because there are no systemic symptoms.","concepts":{"cancer":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":54,"text":"invasive breast cancer"}]},"metastasis":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"surgery":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":54,"text":"resected left breast primary"}]},"chemotherapy":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":54,"text":"adjuvant chemotherapy"}]},"radiation":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"lymph_nodes_removed":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":54,"text":"sentinel node sampling"}]}},"cancer_status":["current"],"cancer_mentions":[{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":54,"text":"she has a resected left breast primary with hormone receptor positive, HER2-negative disease and node-negative status after sentinel node sampling"}],"status":"current","affected_tissue":"left breast","metastasis":false}],"flags":["breast cancer","hormone receptor positive","HER2-negative","node-negative","genomic assay","adjuvant chemotherapy","oncology consultation"]}
{"note_id":55,"date":"2025-04-10","note_type":"Systemic Therapy Note","content":"Genomic assay returned in the intermediate-high range, and adjuvant chemotherapy was recommended. Docetaxel/cyclophosphamide cycle 1 was administered on 2025-04-10. She tolerated infusion with expected fatigue and transient metallic taste, no febrile symptoms. Radiation oncology referral placed for adjuvant whole-breast radiation after completion of chemotherapy. Endocrine therapy to follow radiation. The patient asked whether the in situ component changes the main diagnosis; we reviewed that the invasive component drives prognosis and treatment planning.","summary":"Genomic assay showed intermediate-high risk and adjuvant chemotherapy with docetaxel/cyclophosphamide was initiated; the patient tolerated the first cycle with expected fatigue and metallic taste. A radiation oncology referral was placed for whole‑breast radiation after chemotherapy, with endocrine therapy planned thereafter. The patient was counseled that the invasive component, not the in‑situ component, drives prognosis and treatment planning.","concepts":{"cancer":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":55,"text":"adjuvant chemotherapy was recommended"},{"note_id":55,"text":"Docetaxel/cyclophosphamide cycle 1 was administered on 2025-04-10"},{"note_id":55,"text":"Radiation oncology referral placed for adjuvant whole-breast radiation after completion of chemotherapy"},{"note_id":55,"text":"the invasive component drives prognosis"}]},"metastasis":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"surgery":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"chemotherapy":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":55,"text":"Docetaxel/cyclophosphamide cycle 1 was administered on 2025-04-10"}]},"radiation":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":55,"text":"Radiation oncology referral placed for adjuvant whole-breast radiation after completion of chemotherapy"}]},"lymph_nodes_removed":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]}},"cancer_status":["current"],"cancer_mentions":[{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":55,"text":"adjuvant whole-breast radiation"}],"status":"current","affected_tissue":"breast","metastasis":false}],"flags":["genomic assay","adjuvant chemotherapy","docetaxel/cyclophosphamide","radiation referral","endocrine therapy","invasive carcinoma"]}

